{
  "step_by_step_reasoning": "The visual architecture on the whiteboard depicts a property listing ingestion and dispatcher system divided into three main columns: legacy, dispatcher, and importer. A scheduled CloudWatch Event triggers a Lambda function in the dispatcher microservice to pull listing data from a legacy Monolith DB (represented as RDS) and store it into DynamoDB. Changes in DynamoDB trigger a second Lambda function via DynamoDB Streams, which forwards curated data through API Gateway into the importer microservice. An importer Lambda function saves data into an internal DynamoDB table and invokes AWS Step Functions to orchestrate data enrichment. Upon completion, Step Functions publishes events to Amazon SNS.",
